WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.320
Привет!

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.800
Это означает Хэлло и Нрашин.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.820
Welcome back to привет русский, эпизод Тартиту.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.000
Today is the 2nd June of the 26th of the year, and I am Olya.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.540
We are heading straight into our space adventure, so let's go.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.700
Our word of the day is cosmos, say it slowly with me.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.360
Cosmos.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:17.720
Now a little faster.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:18.340
Cosmos.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:23.280
It means space, and it sounds exactly like the English word cosmos, so you already know it.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.500
Here is a simple sentence.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.120
Я смотрю на космос.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.760
That means I look at space.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:28.960
Repeat after me.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.420
Я смотрю на космос.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.080
Taking a moment to say this sentence out loud helps you picture the night sky, and gives

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.040
you a ready phrase you can use whenever you point upward with a Russian speaking friend

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:39.940
or family member.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.620
Now that we have the big picture, let's zoom in on the things we actually see up there.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.440
The first one is звезда.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:47.540
Say it slowly.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:48.800
звезда.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.060
It means star.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.260
Repeat after me.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:51.980
звезда.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.720
A bright star looks like this.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.020
звезда яркая.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.780
That means the star is bright.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.820
Knowing the word for star lets you describe what you notice on a clear evening,

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.020
torning a quiet moment outside into a chance to practice Russian while you look up.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.560
Next comes Raketa.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.420
Say it with me.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.120
Rakie.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:08.580
Это.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:09.960
This word means rocket.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.120
Repeat after me.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:11.800
Raketa.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.380
Here is how we use it.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.740
Raketa lit it in cosmos.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.800
That means the rocket flies into space.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.860
Learning this word matters because it connects the idea of powerful machines with the destination

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.820
we just learned, helping you tell simple stories about travel beyond Earth.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.660
Our next word is Luna.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:28.460
Luna.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:29.640
It means moon.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:30.720
Repeat after me.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:31.180
Luna.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.720
The moon looks round.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.820
So we say Luna.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:34.480
Krugle.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.080
That means the moon is round.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.500
This word is especially handy when you want to talk about what changes in the sky each

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.200
night, giving you one more tool to describe the world around you in Russian.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:45.680
Now try planeta.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.660
Пла не ета.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.740
It means planet.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:49.940
Repeat after me.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:50.740
Планета.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.340
Earth is one of them.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.080
Земля это планета.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.140
Это значит, что Earth is a planet.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.780
Once you know this, you can start placing our own home in the larger picture we're building,

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.720
which makes the whole topic feel more real and close.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.680
Here comes Сонца.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:06.920
So ленца.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.480
This word means sun.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:09.580
Repeat after me.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.240
Сонца.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.380
We can say, Сонца светит.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:13.640
That means the sun shines.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.940
Adding the sun to our collection lets you talk about what lights up the daytime sky.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.400
Rounding out the set of words you need for any conversation about day or night.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.140
Our last new word is космонавт.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.260
Космо-нафт.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.080
It means космонавт, or astronaut.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.500
Repeat after me.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.560
Космонавт.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.640
We put it in a sentence like this.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.260
Космонавт в космосе.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.640
That means the космонавт is in space.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.480
Knowing this word connects the people who travel with the place they visit so you can picture

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.420
the full story of exploration whenever the topic comes up.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.960
Many space words in Russian are feminine.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.660
They often end in the letter A or A.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.960
Ракета, звезда, и планета are all feminine.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.000
We say, большая ракета to mean big rocket.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.680
The word большая matches the feminine ending.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.000
English does not change words this way,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.840
but Russian likes to match them like team jerseys.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.560
Paying attention to these endings helps your sentences sound natural.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.020
So listeners immediately understand what you are describing without stopping to guess.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.820
Рашен feel very proud of their space story.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:19.900
In 1961, космонот Юрий Гагарин became the first human in space.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.740
Every year on April 12, people celebrate космонотик's day with special shows and museum trips.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.380
Many children in Russia dream of becoming космонавтый one day.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.840
Hearing this history shows why the topic still sparks excitement across generations

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.000
and gives you a real reason to remember the words we practiced.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.780
Now it is practice time.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.240
Если вы устроите today,

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.320
скачай ракета и звезда,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.260
then say, each Russian word out loud as you write it.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.800
Если вы скачаетесь tonight,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.020
then look up and say,

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.280
я вижу звезду, три часа,

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.780
then say, я вижу Луну, три часа.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:53.840
Дискли к активиде,

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.440
стор нововокабillary into something you actually do,

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.220
локим the words into memory through movement and sight.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.620
Want to know a secret about one of our words?

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.900
Ракета и the English word rocket

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.340
are actually the same word.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.940
They both began as the Italian word rocket.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.640
Meaning little spindle,

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.520
because only rockets looked like tiny spools of thread.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.940
The word travels through French and German

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.300
before landing in both Russian and English

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.420
around the same time.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.840
Here is the fun part.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.040
In some situations,

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:24.400
the Russian word rocket can also mean a badminton shuttlecock.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.280
Next time you watch a rocket launch,

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.140
remember it shares a family story

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.920
with that little Italian spindle.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.660
Understanding this shared path

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.320
makes the word feel less foreign

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.920
and more like a friendly traveler

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.820
that belongs to several languages at one.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:37.820
Молодец,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.420
that means well done.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.420
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.660
Practice staying today's words out loud,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:45.640
even just once,

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.740
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.340
See you next time, пока!

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.920
That's Russian for buy.

